---
title: "Our history"
---

_"...the Gruppo Alpinistico Presolana of Scanzorosciate was founded on 2 December 1967... many mountain lovers immediately joined the initiative with enthusiasm."_

The path of the **GAP** now stretches back almost fifty years: the enthusiasm of its founding and of discovering the mountains together, the first adventures outside Italy, and the reputation our strongest members built in the Bergamo climbing scene.

Then came the spread of "going to the mountains" through the town, in every season and every alpine discipline, and the move towards younger people with youth alpinism and the slogan "in the mountains with us". Then the Kilimanjaro adventure, with a group of under-18s on the summit at Christmas 1996.

And then the group's "adult age": the new clubhouse in the town park, the new statute and a role in the community that is now widely recognised, and our present days: demanding, communicative, challenging...

The mountains don't only mean trails or easy glaciers: our members' ascents also include walls, ridges and the hardest, most demanding routes, reaching even the highest peaks of the Alps and, on some occasions, beyond Europe, with the GAP name on the Andes, in Tibet, Patagonia, the Himalaya, the Caucasus and Africa...

The GAP took its first steps on the trails outside our doors, and went on to the most famous treks of the Alps. From Triglav to Monviso, via Monte Rosa, the Tour du Mont Blanc and the Aiguille d'Argentière, without forgetting Badile and the Central Alps. It tackled the equipped trails of the spectacular Dolomites with enthusiasm and explored the Apennines and Central Italy, reaching Gran Sasso, Assisi, Argentario, the islands of the Tuscan Archipelago and Corsica.

The most motivated also took part in treks in the Cordillera Blanca (Peru) and the Annapurna (Nepal).
